<title>GERMANY: Germans seek intervention barley/rye exports.</title>
<headline>Germans seek intervention barley/rye exports.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders placed bids to export 116,000 tonnes of barley and 48,000 tonnes of rye from intervention stores to third countries, grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The EU Cereals Management Committee will decide on the bids later today.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
